                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "For less than a dollar, Gun-Running War Dogs delivers exactly what it promises: a stripped-down Dope Wars-style trading loop where you buy low, sell high, and occasionally gun down anyone who tries to rob you. The buy-sell-upgrade cycle is genuinely addictive in short bursts — watching your profit margins grow and decking out your office with bodyguards and ridiculous furniture has its own charm. That said, once you figure out the optimal strategy, the depth dries up fast, and a few nasty bugs (including a game-breaking error popup in the endgame) can cut your run short in frustrating ways. If you snag it on sale for under a buck and go in expecting a casual clicker with a spreadsheet UI rather than a deep simulation, you'll probably squeeze a few fun hours out of it.",
